SN AutoMessage v2.1

The concept behind this one is basically the same as CNet's news files, with
one exception.  This file is displayed everytime someone logs on, no matter
how often or how many times they've seen it before, until you edit, redo or
nuke it completely.

Handy for things you can never emphasize enough...  (Use your imagination.)

Quick & Easy Installation:

 1  Place it somewhere.  (PFiles: would be good.)

 2  The following options are the default, straight-out-of-the-archive
    settings:  (You may edit these options, but nothing else!  See note
    below...)

    edac=31 /* Min Access to Edit/Kill */
    ulogs=1 /* Enable SN UserLogs? 1=Yes */
    ansi=1  /* Show ANSI? 1=Yes */

 3  At the bottom of the "3; Main prompt" items in bbsmenu, add the
    following line:

    AUTO  |{#0SN:SN_AutoMessage}

    Modify the path to suit and remember, \ = CTRL-Y and { = CTRL-Q.

 4  Reload your bbstext/bbsmenu via CNet's Control Panel menu (option
    #3, "Text/menu reload  RAmiga-T" and you're all set!

 5  Be sure and let everyone know that the option is available.  (Add it
    to your menu.)  Until they manually change it, they'll get the prompt.
    So it acts normal...

(This sucker wasn't big enough to deserve it's own .guide, installer, icons,
help file, blah blah blah plus tax...)

Midnight

NOTE:   I haven't worried about the little files I've released (the ones
